* Generate an Ed25519 key
Choose a new filename to keep existing keys. ssh-keygen prompts for a passphrase.
@code bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C 'your-email@example.com' -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_example
@end
Share only the `.pub` file. Keep the private key on the client.

* Load the key into an existing SSH agent
@code bash
ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_example
ssh-add -l
@end
An SSH agent must already be running in this session.

Reference: {https://man.openbsd.org/ssh-keygen}[ssh-keygen].
